  "answer_text": "Unfortunately, the Indiana Pacers are **not** in the 2026 NBA Playoffs. The Indiana Pacers missed the playoffs for the first time since 2023.\n\nThe full-year absence of Tyrese Haliburton, who was sidelined with a torn Achilles tendon sustained in Game 7 of the 2025 NBA Finals, along with a handful of other injuries caused catastrophe upon the Pacers' chances in their post-NBA Finals season. Key players in Aaron Nesmith, Obi Toppin, and Ben Sheppard also missed significant time due to injuries, which plagued Indiana's record.\n\nIt's worth noting that the Pacers were the defending Eastern Conference champions \u2014 the Thunder won the franchise's first NBA title since relocating from Seattle to Oklahoma City last year, beating the Indiana Pacers in a seven-game Finals that went right down to the wire.\n\nThe current 2026 NBA Finals features the **New York Knicks vs. the San Antonio Spurs**, with the Knicks currently leading two games to none.",
